\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Continues Quietly  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2 : Traders \b0\par\par\uc2 171 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 1995\par 09:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-DJ)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues quietly buying dollars late in Asian dealings Thursday, traders in Tokyo said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market throughout the day, helping to keep a floor under the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which at 0742 GMT, is trading at 1.3765 Deutsche marks and 87.65 yen. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  quietly - making relatively small dollar-yen purchases - to create the impression there is more 'natural' buying support for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  than is actually the case. \par \par \uc2  One market source in Tokyo estimated the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already spent about $500 million Thursday to keep the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  afloat. \par \par \uc2  'That ($500 million) sounds like a pretty good guess to me,' a source at another Tokyo bank said. \par \par \uc2  But traders also said the dollar is supported by real buying interest from a variety of participants at its current levels. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-07-95 \par \par \uc2  0744GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr7k05gap\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
