\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  market snubs BOJ as dollar slides one yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoshiko Mori \par \uc2 589 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 19 (Reuter) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market snubbed Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, knocking the dollar down by more than one full yen despite a sharp warning that market players could be burnt if they bet on a weaker dollar. \par \par \uc2  Waves of selling -- triggered by fading market hopes that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would soon recover to 90 yen -- overwhelmed the dollar, which fell to 87.27 yen in late Tokyo trade after closing at about 88.40 yen in New York on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had risen to a 3-1/2 month high of 89.27 yen on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's slide was a slap in the face for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had come out with some unusually tough words earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  "A temporary correction of the dollar's rise cannot be avoided to some extent, but market operators who try to reverse the recent trend (of a rising dollar) will certainly be disappointed -- and they will get burnt," a senior Bank of Japan (BOJ) official told Reuters on Wednesday morning. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ will make its utmost efforts to ensure an orderly reversal of the dollar," he added. \par \par \uc2  The comments -- backed by intermittent dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- were unusually forthright for a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which typically confines itself to more cryptic remarks. \par \par \uc2  But senior bankers said Japan's recent bold attempt to push the dollar back above 90 yen had backfired and might well be undermining the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's natural rise. \par \par \uc2  "Efforts to push up the dollar have got to the stage where they may undermine its natural upward correction," said Yukuo Takahashi, managing director of Chemical Bank's Tokyo branch. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been strengthening after the United States and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy it on July 7. The joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which came after Washington and Tokyo moved in tandem to ease credit, persuaded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets they had agreed on the need for a stronger dollar. \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministry bureaucrats have been busy persuading Japanese institutional investors that the dollar would recover to 90-95 yen in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Japanese government sources told Reuters on Tuesday Japan had set a near-term target for the dollar of about 90 yen. The United States "understands" Tokyo's position, they added. \par \par \uc2  Some sources said a rise in the dollar to only around 90 yen would not be enough to support Japan's troubled economy, but they declined to specify any target beyond that level. \par \par \uc2  The sources also said Japan would step into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if needed to attain the target. But bankers said BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was losing the power to boost the dollar in the face of fading hopes that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would jump the 90-yen hurdle. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is losing power as market hopes for a dollar recovery to above 90 yen recede," said Yoshimori Matsushita, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Mitsubishi Bank. \par \par \uc2  "The Fed (Federal Reserve) needs to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  now to give evidence of the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 -U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  initiative," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market technical analysts had already said the dollar was likely to drift lower before starting another rally. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rally, which had cheered the Tokyo stock market, had been good news for Finance Minister Masayoshi Takemura, who also heads the smallest partner in Prime Minister Tomiichi Murayama's ruling coalition. The coalition faces a key electoral test in Upper House polls on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr7j05rot\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
