\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr Sinks On Unfavorable U.S. Trade Data: World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By JOSEPH REBELLO \par \uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 1995\par 22:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (AP-DJ)--The dollar sank Tuesday, weighed down by a report that showed a widening U.S. trade deficit and by growing skepticism about the effectiveness of Japan's efforts to bolster the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Increasingly cool to \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar fell steadily against the yen - a trend it mimicked against the Deutsche mark. Traders attributed the decline to profit-taking by nervous investors. \par \par \uc2  'Because we saw so many up days in a row, people decided to take their profits off the table before they saw a rout in the dollar,' said Seth Cohen, a director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Merrill Lynch Inc. in New York. \par \par \uc2  Traders said investors' confidence was also shaken by data that showed the U.S. trade deficit swelled to $11.43 billion in May from a revised $11.42 billion in April. Market expectations had called for the deficit to shrink to $10.42 billion. \par \par \uc2  Those numbers defied assertions by U.S. officials - most recently by Alice Rivlin, director of the Office of Management and Budget - that the weak dollar is helping to trim the trade deficit. The dollar later fell to intraday lows of 1.3855 marks and 88.20 yen. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also proved stubbornly resistant to efforts by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push it higher. Despite two \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar failed to perk up. Traders said investors increasingly think the bank is overdoing its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts. \par \par \uc2  'The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  so often now it's become almost routine,' said Marc Chandler, a senior analyst at Deutsche Bank. 'They can now \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  all they want and it's not going to have any effect.' \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar was quoted at 1.3885 Deutsche marks, down from 1.3955 marks late Monday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also quoted at 88.37 yen, down from 88.82 yen. Sterling was trading at $1.5943, down from $1.5954. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-07-95 \par \par \uc2  2052GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr7i05gy4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
