\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 -2: Swiss Rate Cut Moved Dlr to Intraday Highs \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 1995\par 22:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The prospect of a German interest rate cut had buoyed the dollar since July 7, when the Federal Reserve and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the dollar up. Many traders interpreted the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as evidence of a multinational effort to bolster the dollar. \par \par \uc2  They reasoned that if Japan and the U.S. were acting in concert, Germany wouldn't be long in joining the effort by cutting rates. Germany, in any case, had endorsed statements made by the Group of Seven industrial nations that the U.S. dollar was undervalued. \par \par \uc2  'It seemed like something coordinated was going on,' said Robert Near, a vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at the Bank of New York. 'The Fed had cut interest rates, and the Bank of Japan cut interest rates. So you had the feeling that G-7 central banks were changing from an anti-inflation stance to a pro-growth stance.' \par \par \uc2  That faith had led many traders to conclude that the dollar's long-term decline against the mark and yen had ended. \par \par \uc2  Admittedly, expectations for a Bundesbank rate cut were shaken somewhat on Wednesday, when final data were released showing western Germany's consumer price index rose 2.4% in June on an annual basis, slightly more than the 2.3% gain shown in the preliminary estimate. \par \par \uc2  But traders' reticence didn't last long. Early Thursday, Switzerland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its largely symbolic discount rate by 0.50 percentage points to 2.50%. Since the Swiss National Bank usually moves in tandem with the Bundesbank, expectations once more grew for a German rate cut. \par \par \uc2  The dollar spiked to intraday highs of 1.4150 marks and 88.47 yen shortly after the Swiss rate cut. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-07-95 \par \par \uc2  2053GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr7d058q5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
