\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr Slumps on Dashed Hopes For German Rate Cut: World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By JOSEPH REBELLO \par \uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 1995\par 22:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (AP-DJ)--The dollar slumped against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, crushed by disappointed expectations for an interest-rate cut in Germany. \par \par \uc2  Although the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to hold broadly steady against the yen, the Deutsche Bundesbank's decision to keep rates unchanged sent the dollar into a tailspin that was arrested only by fears that central banks might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the fall. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless the decline wiped out nearly all the gains the dollar had eked out against the mark since the Federal Reserve and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  July 7 to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It also prompted traders to reassess their belief that the dollar's long-term decline against the mark and the yen had come to a halt. 'Today's the last day you'll hear anyone say the dollar has bottomed out,' said Bruce Campbell, chief dealer for First Fidelity Bank Corp. in Newark, N.J. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar was quoted at 1.3891 Deutsche marks, well down from 1.4030 marks late Wednesday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also quoted at 87.40 yen, little changed from 87.43 yen. Sterling was trading at $1.5998, up from $1.5915. \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank decision, made at the last meeting of its policy-setting council before a four-week recess, buoyed the mark against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Despite rising complaints from German corporations that the strong mark is hurting revenues, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it couldn't ease rates because inflation remained a threat. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-07-95 \par \par \uc2  2052GMT \par \par \uc2  (Corrected 1736EDT) \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr7d058pw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
