\par\par \b \uc2  Japan ODR decision up to BOJ -- MOF vice minister. \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 10 (Reuter) - Any decision on a change in Japan's official discount rate is up to the Bank of Japan (BOJ), Vice Finance Minister Kyosuke Shinozawa told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  He also said the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the United States to push up the dollar last Friday was in line with an agreement reached by the Group of Seven (G7) industrial nations on April 25. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's announcement on Friday that it would guide short-term money market interest rates lower was a reflection of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's basic stand of flexible and timely monetary measures when required. "I believe the BOJ will continue to take that stance," Shinozawa said. \par \par \uc2  Asked if his ministry wanted the BOJ to change its monetary policy, Shinozawa said, "Any change in the discount rate is up to the BOJ, and we will continue to watch the BOJ's judgement." \par \par \uc2  Commenting on the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. Federal Reserve later on Friday, Shinozawa said, "Japan and the United States shared the same opinion." \par \par \uc2  Shinozawa said the effects of the BOJ's move to steer interest rates lower would spread to various sectors of the economy. "We will keep watching such effects," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by G7 countries on May 31 and by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. on Friday was based on the April 25 accord struck by G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors, calling for an "orderly reversal" of the dollar, Shinozawa said. \par \par \uc2  The April agreement was reaffirmed last month at the Halifax summit of G7 leaders. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr7a066b3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
