\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Midday: Japanese Exporters Eye 88.00-Yen Level \b0\par\par\uc2 182 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 1995\par 04:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders are mixed on the long-term impact of the concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Federal Reserve last Friday. \par \par \uc2  'The impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 's been exaggerated,' said a trader at a major Japanese commercial bank. \par \par \uc2  He said the joint effort by the Japanese and U.S. central banks to buy dollars last Friday only lifted the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 0.50 yen or so. \par \par \uc2  He added that the dollar must breach resistance around 87.15 yen before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be ruled successful. \par \par \uc2  The trader said, however, that the dollar remains bullish and Japanese exporters are hesitant to sell dollars at the present level of around 87.00 yen. He said they would wait until the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  enters the threshold of 88.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso is mostly unchanged from levels earlier in the day despite dollar-buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Around 0216 GMT, the dollar is trading at 25.55 Philippine pesos. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-07-95 \par \par \uc2  0217GMT \par \par \uc2  1046 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr7a0552u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
