\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2: European Were Out But Not Indifferent \b0\par\par\uc2 258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 1995\par 20:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Officials at various European central banks said they weren't participating in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and traders in Frankfurt said there was no sign of the Bundesbank in the market, something that was confirmed by U.S. and Japanese officials. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was fairly light, with only purchases of about $10 million at a time. \par \par \uc2  The absence of European central banks Friday is cited by authorities as evidence that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflected primarily Japanese concerns about prospective dollar movements. But officials stress that the absence of European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action shouldn't be interpreted as a lack of concern about substantive dollar weakness. \par \par \uc2  Japan, the U.S. and five other major industrial nations reaffirmed last month a commitment to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, if necessary. And the leaders of the so-called Group of Seven nations also stressed the need for an 'orderly reversal' of recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements. \par \par \uc2  U.S. officials suggest that while Japan's concerns over short-term dollar movements aren't fully shared in Washington, coordinated U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has some collateral benefits. \par \par \uc2  By \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the dollar was firm, if not on a slight upward intraday trend, the Fed and Bank of Japan have helped to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders on edge. \par \par \uc2  And by keeping markets guessing, rather than accurately predicting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , U.S. and other authorities believe that the actions will have some impact on signaling appropriate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-07-95 \par \par \uc2  1842GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr77054dk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
