\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ's June dollar purchases estimated at $1.33 bln. \b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 30 (Reuter) - The Bank of Japan (BOJ) bought an estimated $1.33 billion through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June, sharply up from $84 million in the previous month, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The figures include the last two trading days of the previous month, but not the last two business days of this month, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlements are made two days after transactions. \par \par \uc2  BOJ data, released on Friday, showed that capital outlays from the government's special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to the private sector totalled 112.0 billion yen in June. \par \par \uc2  The figure is comprised mostly of yen payments from the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to the private sector, mainly commercial banks. Those yen payments are the result of the BOJ's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, raises yen cash for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by issuing special financing bills (FBs) for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Those FBs are also used to convert dollar-denominated income gains on the government external reserves into yen. \par \par \uc2  Outstanding FBs as of June 30 total 24.02 trillion yen, up by 157.0 billion yen from a month earlier. \par \par \uc2  On May 31, a surprise joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Federal Reserve, the Bundesbank, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and several European central banks lifted the dollar by about two yen to above 85 yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 84.80/90 yen at 1000 GMT on Friday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr6u06ffk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
