\par\par \b \uc2  Japan MOF watching yen impact on economy - Takemura. \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 2 (Reuter) - Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely watching, with concern, the impact of the recent rise of the yen on Japan's economy, Finance Minister Masayoshi Takemura told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  He also said the ministry is working on drafting comprehensive measures to tackle the problem of bad loans held by financial instititutions within a set period of time, but he declined to say when the ministry will finalise the package. \par \par \uc2  Asked what he thinks about using taxpayers' money to to tackle the bad loan problem, Takemura said: "It is important to protect Japan's financial system." \par \par \uc2  "In this sense public involvement in a general sense would naturally be an important theme," Takemura added. \par \par \uc2  In an economic package unveiled in April as part of an effort to tackle the high yen, the government promised to strive to deal with the problem of bad loans within five years. \par \par \uc2  On the subject of Wednesday's concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Takemura said joint resolve between \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the United States formed the basis of the move, and European central banks later joined the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after having been contacted by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the United States. \par \par \uc2  Three days before the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  started to worry about yet another rise in the yen and started to conduct an intense dialogue with the United States over the timing of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Takemura said. \par \par \uc2  Initially the United States was cautious but gradually it became positive towards \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Takemura said. The U.S. and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  contacted Europe about joining in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , therefore this agreement between \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. made the broad \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  possible, he added. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr620794f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
