\par\par \b \uc2  Japan's Foreign Reserves -4: Rises For 19th Straight Time \b0\par\par\uc2 202 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 1995\par 11:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The May rise was the 19th consecutive monthly increase for Japan and set another record for the most foreign reserves held by a single country, the official said. \par \par \uc2  April's big rise was the second largest ever recorded by Japan and was fueled by consistent and large-scale dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  During that month the dollar fell to its lowest level against the yen since the establishment of modern exchange rates in the late 1940s, hitting 79.75 yen on April 19. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was spotted buying dollars in world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in May as well, however, with considerably less frequency than in April, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers. \par \par \uc2  Referring to Wednesday's joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  led by the U.S. Federal Reserve, the Deutsche Bundesbank and the BOJ, which took place in early New York trading, the official said the coordinated action was 'clearly effective,' noting that the dollar climbed briefly to 85.40 yen from its levels in the high 82-yen range at the time the buying occurred. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-06-95 \par \par \uc2  0941GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr61042tc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
