\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ's May dollar purchases estimated at $84 mln. \b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 31 (Reuter) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) bought an estimated $84 million through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in May, down sharply from $11.78 billion in April, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  Because \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlements are made two days after the transactions, the figures include the last two trading days of the previous month and do not include the last two business days of the current month. \par \par \uc2  BOJ data released on Wednesday showed that capital outlays from the government's special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to the private sector totalled seven billion yen in May. \par \par \uc2  The figure is made up mostly of yen payments from the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account to the private sector, mainly commercial banks. The yen payments are a result of BOJ dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, raises yen in cash for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by issuing special financing bills (FBs) for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The FBs are also used for converting dollar-denominated income gains on the government's external reserves into yen. \par \par \uc2  The outstanding total of FBs as of Wednesday was 23.86 trillion yen, up about 284 billion yen from a month earlier. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the fall in BOJ dollar purchases in May was mainly because of the dollar's recovery against the yen after it hit a record low of 79.75 yen on April 19. \par \par \uc2  The dollar clawed back to as high as 87.75 yen in May. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ bought a record $14.07 billion in March. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr5v07bgg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
