\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Central bank \highlight\uc2  dlr asset selloff seen in 1995 - IBJ. \b0\par\par\uc2 241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 25 (Reuter) - The rapid rise of dollar assets in the hands of central banks following the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the first quarter of 1995 may result in the sale of those assets later this year, the Industrial Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a note to investors. \par \par \uc2  "Such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has temporarily boosted central banks' dollar holdings, reversing the trend towards increasing the share of non-dollar reserve assets," the IBJ said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter wild \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market swings has pushed official reserves to new highs, with those for G7 states rising to $1.2 trillion from $975 billion at end 1993. \par \par \uc2  IBJ sees at least sales of $20 billion of dollar assets, mostly short-dated treasuries, unless the recent strength of the dollar is sustained by stabilisation of the U.S. position as a net debtor. \par \par \uc2  "Substantial (but quiet) dollar sales will be a feature of capital flows later this year." \par \par \uc2  While \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil and generally bearish market sentiment has reduced international flows of capital, to $215 in 1994 from $380 billion in 1993, the IBJ sees a gradual recovery this year. \par \par \uc2  "The passion for foreign securities seen in 1993 has been replaced by a more cautious selection of foreign investments... Confidence will take time to rebuild but flows should be on a rising trend in 1995," IBJ said. \par \par \uc2  -- London newsroom 44 171 542 5887 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995