\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Debt -2-: Investors Buy Ahead Of Bond Redemption \b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 1995\par 09:32\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  In addition, many corporate issues are usually redeemed between May and July, reducing supply burden in the market, the general manager at the securities unit of the major bank. \par \par \uc2  The deputy manager at the big bank says with the redemption of five-year bank debentures later this month, investors are looking for the best possible alternative to fill the gap with the high coupon these debentures produced, amid sharp declines in Japanese interest rates since the beginning of 1995. "Right now, it seems reasonable to buy new issues at near par," he says. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  the money market at its usual \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  time, surprising many market participants who expected an addition of funds to boost bank reserves. \par \par \uc2  This follows excessively generous money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. Traders say Wednesday's move was probably aimed at protesting a report in the financial daily, Nihon Keizai Shimbun, speculating that the Bank of Japan was trying to lead short-term interest rates slightly higher to prepare for an easing when necessary. \par \par \uc2  Despite this irregularity in money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders say it is premature to conclude that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is changing the recent range of key unsecured overnight call money rate - which has remained around 1 9/32% and 1 11/32%. \par \par \uc2  The unsecured overnight call rate rose as high as 1 12/32% this session, but is currently at 1 11/32%, up from 1 9/32% late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Rates for new three-month certificates of deposit is unchanged from late Wednesday at 1.34%. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is now trading at 87.16 yen, up from 86.85 yen in New York late Wednesday and also above 86.62 yen late in Tokyo Wednesday. The Nikkei stock index ended the session down 158.79 points at 16,312.56. \par \par \uc2  A weaker yen is bearish for bonds as it reduces the value of yen-denominated assets in comparison to assets in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Weaker stocks, on the other hand, are bullish for bonds as it keeps pressure for an accommodative monetary stance. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) DOW JONES NEWS 05-18-95 \par \par \uc2  0332EDT \par \par \uc2  4077 4153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011024dr5i0188s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
