\par\par \b \uc2  Japan Debt -2-: Sanyo Elect, Tohoku Elect Power Offer Bonds \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 1995\par 05:00\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't enter the money market at its usual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  time, surprising many market participants who expected an addition of funds to boost bank reserves, which is currently 90 billion yen above the requirement. \par \par \uc2  This follows excessively generous money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday. Traders say Wednesday's move was probably aimed at protesting a report in the financial daily, Nihon Keizai Shimbun, speculating that the Bank of Japan was trying to lead short-term interest rates slightly higher to prepare for an easing when necessary. \par \par \uc2  "This irregularity in money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  is nothing new. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shouldn't confuse market participants and let them start to speculate about their intentions," the chief dealer at the securities unit of a major bank says. \par \par \uc2  The key unsecured overnight call money rate rose as high as 1 12/32% from 1 9/32% late Wednesday, and up 2/32% from earlier Thursday. The unsecured overnight call rate is currently at 1 11/32%. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is now trading at 86.95 yen, up from 86.85 yen in New York late Wednesday and also above 86.62 yen late in Tokyo Wednesday. The Nikkei stock index ended the morning session down 261.39 points at 16,309.96. \par \par \uc2  A weaker yen is bearish for bonds as it reduces the value of yen-denominated assets in comparison to assets in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Weaker stocks, on the other hand, are bullish for bonds as it keeps pressure for an accommodative monetary stance. \par \par \uc2  This session, Tohoku Electric Power Co. is offering in Japan 50 billion yen of 3.05% seven-year bonds at par, while Sanyo Electric Co. is also offering in Japan 20 billion yen of 2.85% five-year bonds and 10 billion yen of 3.05% six-year bonds, both at the issue price of 100. \par \par \uc2  Later this session, Toyo Suisan Kaisha Ltd. is seen pricing 20 billion to 30 billion yen of six-year or seven-year bonds via lead manager Nikko Securities Co. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 05-17-95 \par \par \uc2  2300EDT \par \par \uc2  4077 4153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011024dr5i0186l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
