\par\par \b \uc2  Japan in quandary over value of dollar reserves. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kazuhiko Tamaki \par \uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 26 (Reuter) - Japan's finance ministry has its back to the wall as it seeks ways of coping with the impact of the declining dollar on the value of its external reserves, government sources said. \par \par \uc2  Amid renewed dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) to prop up the dollar, Japan cannot rapidly shift part of its reserves to gold or to other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the mark. "Unrealised losses on external reserves have swelled, but there is no quick remedy for the situation," a government official told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Japan's external reserves stood at a record high of $141.52 billion at end-March, mainly due to aggressive dollar buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said that as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) invests the bulk of the reserves in U.S. Treasury securities, it has suffered huge losses with the dollar's protracted drop against the yen. \par \par \uc2  More than 90 percent of Japan's foreign reserves are believed to be held in dollars, compared with an average 60 percent in other industrialised countries. \par \par \uc2  The dollar plunged to a postwar low of 79.75 yen on April 19 and continues to hover weakly around 82 yen. \par \par \uc2  A senior figure in the largest party in Japan's ruling coalition, Koichi Kato, said the MOF is cautious about proposals from within the party to switch some of Japan's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves out of dollars into marks or gold. \par \par \uc2  "The finance ministry is very, very cautious about that kind of drastic policy change, but we have to convey complaints from our constituents to the government," Kato said. \par \par \uc2  Kato said in an interview that the Liberal Democratic Party (LDP) had received complaints from the public about the drop in value of Japan's foreign reserves due to the dollar's fall of more than 20 percent against the yen this year. \par \par \uc2  According to the MOF, unrealised losses on its special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account are expected to be around 9.85 trillion yen ($120 billion) at the end of March 1996. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ, which bought an estimated $14 billion in March, a monthly record, conducts \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by using funds from the MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounts. \par \par \uc2  Senior government officials have discussed whether to increase the proportion of German government bonds in the reserves, but could not reach a consensus, the official said. \par \par \uc2  Such a move could accelerate the mark's rise and have a negative impact on German exporters, the source said. \par \par \uc2  There are liquidity problems in buying assets of other European countries, the source added. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, increasing the amount of gold in the reserves is not a realistic possibility as such moves would be easily detected by the market. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has 819 tonnes of gold, which accounts for about 1.2 percent of the nation's external reserves. \par \par \uc2  The MOF does not normally comment on the management of its external reserves. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masayoshi Takemura told parliament recently that for Japan alone to increase its gold holdings would not be desirable. \par \par \uc2  The head of MOF's international affairs bureau, Takatoshi Kato, also said reducing dollar holdings is an issue that needs to be considered on a long-term basis. \par \par \uc2  A senior MOF official told Reuters last week that there has been no policy change in the management of external reserves. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr4q08c6a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
