\par\par \b \uc2  Japan discount rate decision is for BOJ - Takemura. \b0\par\par\uc2 183 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 14 (Reuter) - Finance Minister Masayoshi Takemura told a news conference a decision on the official discount rate is a matter for the Bank of Japan (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  He was replying to a question on why the government had not included discount rate policy in its emergency economic package, unveiled earlier on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "We did not include it (the discount rate) in the package because it is a BOJ matter," Takemura said. \par \par \uc2  He said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to strengthen policy coordination on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with major nations. \par \par \uc2  Asked when the supplementary budget for fiscal 1995/96 will be drafted, Takemura said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) hopes to submit its draft to parliament as soon as possible before the end of May. \par \par \uc2  Takemura said among the highlights of the emergency package were that Japan would make efforts to cut its current account surplus and to get rid of financial institutions' bad loans. \par \par \uc2  "The package contained measures which were drastic compared with what the government has announced in the past," he said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr4e08q7b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
