\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Friday's Japan Stimulus Package Awaited \b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 1995\par 22:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The mark's move higher also came at a time when the yen was depressed by fears that a Japanese stimulus package to be announced Friday may be accompanied by heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and possibly the Federal Reserve, said Amy Smith, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist in New York at I.D.E.A., an analytical firm. \par \par \uc2  Smith noted that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases might have an exaggerated effect in the thin trading conditions likely to prevail on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials have said the stimulus package is designed to stabilize the yen and help companies that have been hurt by the surging Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Other traders said the mark's upward lurch Wednesday was technically driven, and perhaps related to the unwinding of options positions by European players. \par \par \uc2  The mark rally took the dollar down to an intraday low of 1.3957 marks around 1241 GMT. But the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  quickly retreated again, losing much of its gains against the yen and allowing the dollar to move up to an intraday high of 1.4095 marks at 1518 GMT, around midday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the mark was quoted at 59.74 yen, up a little from 59.65 yen late Tuesday but well below an intraday high around 60.25 yen. On Monday, the mark hit a record low of 57.58 yen. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar remains locked in a fairly narrow range between around 1.3950-1.4100 marks, with little incentive to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of those bands as the market winds down ahead of Easter holidays which will see many European centers close for an extended weekend. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-04-95 \par \par \uc2  2035GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr4c02oui\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
