\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr under fierce assault in Asia, below 81.00 yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 10 (Reuter) - The dollar plummeted to a fresh global post-World War Two low on Monday morning, sinking below 81.00 yen as the government pledged again to draw up economic measures to cope with the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said heavy dollar selling by Japanese exporters and U.S. investment funds overwhelmed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The market was full of operators rushing to sell dollars against the yen,'' said a U.S. bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had closed at 83.68/75 yen in New York on Friday, against a high this year of 101.45 yen, posted on January 4 in New York. By around 0200 GMT on Monday, the dollar had clawed back above 81 yen and was trading around 81.40 yen. \par \par \uc2  A big upset for Japan's established parties in local gubernatorial elections in Tokyo and Osaka, both won by former television entertainers running as independents, also undermined sentiment for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Major parties' losses are usually a factor for selling yen, but it increased scepticism that Japan's measures may not halt the yen's rises,'' said a long-term credit bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masayoshi Takemura told reporters on Monday morning that the yen's surge was a serious worry'' for Japan and the government hoped to draw up emergency plans to cope with it this week. \par \par \uc2  Takemura also urged the United States to show a strong stance'' in dealing with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  But economists have said the U.S. Federal Reserve Bank was unlikely to move soon to hike interest rates, one step that might help stem the dollar's decline. \par \par \uc2  Nor have they been overly optimistic about Washington's commitment to cutting its budget and trade deficits, also cited as factors behind the dollar's precipitous drop. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo share prices, initially weakened by the yen's rise, rose smartly in late morning trade on hopes that the government package would include support for the flagging share market. \par \par \uc2  At the Tokyo midday close, the key Nikkei share average was up 152.77 points, or 0.97 pct, at 15,872.27 \par \par \uc2  Economists and government sources have said the economic package was unlikely to contain any miracle cure for the nations's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -induced woes, even if it was twinned with a cut in the Bank of Japan's official discount rate. \par \par \uc2  Government sources said on Friday that the BOJ might cut the discount rate this week, perhaps by 0.75 percentage point from its current record low of 1.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr4a08u48\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
