\par\par \b \uc2  = \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  View -3-: Need Seen For Strong Govt Fiscal Package \b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1995\par 23:43\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Speculation that the Bank of Japan may reduce interest rates has gained momentum, largely due to the belief that a strong yen is more a problem for Japan than for the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Michael Englund, chief economist at MMS International Inc., said data overwhelmingly indicate that the dollar, when compared against a broad basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't, in fact, declining. "There are fewer impending inflation or trade implications from the dollar," Englund said. "The Japanese economy will feel most of the pain from the stronger yen." \par \par \uc2  That, analysts said, could encourage the Japanese government to craft a package of steps to cope with the economic impact of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surge. Such a package could benefit the dollar in the long run, helping to stimulate Japanese growth and ultimately U.S. exports to Japan, reducing the U.S. trade deficit with that country. \par \par \uc2  Following a special meeting of Japanese economic ministers after Friday morning's regular cabinet meeting, top government spokesman Kozo Igarashi said the government wants to come up with a comprehensive stimulus package and will discuss details early next week. \par \par \uc2  But details on what the government will come up with remained scarce Friday. And market observers said no concrete discussions on budgetary needs for a yen-related stimulus package have begun yet. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the government is expected to present a supplementary budget in May to deal with its response to the Jan. 17 earthquake that devastated the Kobe region. Japanese officials indicate that the government's yen package should be ready by the first week of May. \par \par \uc2  Although the outlook for a combined earthquake-yen economic package remains sketchy, signs that a package is coming helped share prices hold fairly steady despite the yen's surge. The Nikkei 225 stock index ended down only 96.37 points to 15,719.50 despite the dollar's plunge to a record low of 83.65 yen, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Technical Data's Berryman said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was abuzz with talk that finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials would meet in London this week to discuss concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and policy coordination ahead of a meeting of Group od Seven finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials slated for April 25. \par \par \uc2  To be sure, she said, monetary authorities are greatly concerned about the dollar's accelerating weakness despite joint dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the central banks of the U.S., \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Germany, and the U.K. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 04-09-95 \par \par \uc2  1743EDT \par \par \uc2  4137 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011024dr4900xvb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
