\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr Mixed On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears, Upcoming Data: World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By ALAN S. CULLISON \par \uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 1995\par 22:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (AP-DJ)--Fears of more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  coupled with position-taking ahead of a key U.S. employment report left the dollar mixed Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Though traders said that sentiment toward the dollar remained bearish, they added that the market was not anxious to tempt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Federal Reserve or other major central banks by trying to take the dollar significantly lower against the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  Traders also noted a reluctance to take major new positions ahead of Friday's release of closely-watched March U.S. employment data. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar continued to fall against the yen, hitting a new post-war low of 85.13 yen near the end of the Asian day, and traders said the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's climb appears impervious to any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The central banks of the U.S., Germany and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday in what appeared a concerted effort to push the dollar higher. On Thursday, there was no sign of dollar buying by the Federal Reserve or the Deutsche Bundesbank, though the Bank of Japan was rumored to have bought dollars again during Asian dealings. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the yen's rise Thursday was also fueled by the lack of progress in talks between the U.S. and Japan on opening up the Japanese auto market. As long as the talks are at an impasse, traders said the market is left with the impression that the U.S. doesn't particularly mind the rise in the yen - which makes Japanese goods less competitive on world markets. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar was quoted at 1.3762 Deutsche marks, up from 1.3725 marks late Thursday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also quoted at 85.40 yen, down from 86.04 yen. Sterling was trading at $1.6065, down from $1.6110. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-04-95 \par \par \uc2  2035GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr4602igb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
