\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr Higher Amid Short-Covering, Fear Of Fed: World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By ALAN S. CULLISON \par \uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 1995\par 22:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (AP-DJ)--The dollar rose unexpectedly Tuesday, as fears of further Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  led to some broad-based buying of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Fed wasn't sighted in the market Tuesday, but traders said Monday's aggressive dollar-buying by the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made market players reluctant to take large short positions in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The scale of Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which involved at least $1 billion of Fed dollar purchases, together with statements from U.S. officials in favor of a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , may have convinced market players that the U.S. is committed to defending the dollar, traders said. \par \par \uc2  'I think that (the dollar recovery) is a sign that the Fed's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was successful,' said Jim Blackwelder, vice president in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at National Westminster USA in New York. 'There was just a crazy tone to the market before, with people ready to sell the dollar on any event whatever. The market blinked, and it was the first time that it blinked in a while.' \par \par \uc2  Though the dollar lunged to a new record low of 85.60 yen very early in Asian dealings, traders said the market clearly had little enthusiasm for the move. \par \par \uc2  Helped back by more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar climbed steadily against the yen and Deutsche mark through most of Asian trading, and continued higher in Europe and the U.S. before it was hit by profit-taking. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar was quoted at 1.3785 Deutsche marks, up from 1.3725 marks late Monday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also quoted at 86.21 yen, up from 86.13 yen. Sterling was trading at $1.6065, down from $1.6195. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-04-95 \par \par \uc2  2042GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr4402edf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
