\par\par \b \uc2  Japan's Foreign Reserves -3: Japan Held Largest Reserves \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1995\par 10:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The finance ministry maintains a policy of not explaining specifically why the level of foreign reserves changes in any month. But market analysts often attribute the rise in part to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, which traders say has been almost a regular occurrence in recent months. \par \par \uc2  An official briefing reporters said the latest figures represent the 13th consecutive month of increases in Japan's foreign reserves. \par \par \uc2  The official said the yen's strongest level in March was 88.16 yen to the dollar, posted March 31, and the yen's weakest level came on March 2 at 96.65 yen to the dollar, during Tokyo dealing hours. \par \par \uc2  The official said that judging from most recent statistics available in each country, Japan holds the largest reserves of any nation. At the end of January, Japan's total foreign reserves stood at $124 billion. Next was Taiwan, which at the end of November, had foreign reserves totalling $93.3 billion. Statistics for Taiwan frequently lag those of other countries. \par \par \uc2  Germany was third with $83.0 billion, and the U.S. had the world's fourth largest reserves of $78.0 billion, both from the end of January. Singapore held the world's fifth highest foreign reserves of $57.7 billion, at the end of November. \par \par \uc2  The latest foreign reserves figures follow the dollar's fall to new postwar lows of 88.23 yen Friday, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the U.S. Federal Reserve in Asian markets Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers say despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Fed's decision to leave interest rates unchanged have left little reason for investors to increase dollar holdings. As such, they expect the dollar to fall further, with some eyeing 85.00 yen has the next crucial support level for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  With the dollar nearing that point already, Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to follow, which should ensure \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves will remain high for the foreseeable future. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-04-95 \par \par \uc2  0801GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr4302cqq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
