\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -2: Weak Japanese Stocks Helped Sink Dlr In Asia \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1995\par 23:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Traders said that the dollar appears to be especially ripe for another fall against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , amid fears of further losses in Tokyo financial markets. The plunging Japanese stock market pressured the dollar during Asian dealings Monday, with the Nikkei index of 225 selected issues closing down 758.66 points at 15,381.29. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that the Nikkei dropped amid fears that the yen's strength, which is likely to be ruinous to Japan's many exporters, will not end any time soon. \par \par \uc2  David DeRosa, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for Swiss Bank Corp. in New York, said that fear has been to some extent self-perpetuating, since each decline in the Nikkei average has led to a new round of yen strength, as Japanese investors struggle to cover their losses by repatriating their overseas investments. \par \par \uc2  'Until they get out of this mess, they will continue to repatriate,' DeRosa said. 'That is why I say that anything bad for the Japanese economy is good for the yen.' \par \par \uc2  In a move that surprised many traders, the Fed staged its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia, buying dollars in three rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that traders said were unusually aggressive. It was the first time that the U.S. Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asian markets since February 1992. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also sighted buying dollars Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action pushed the dollar sharply higher during Asian dealings, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  began to fall back again near the end of the Asian day, as players in Asian markets closed off their positions. \par \par \uc2  The Fed entered the market again during the North American day and around the end of European trading, traders noted, as the market seemed poised to take the dollar down through 86.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-04-95 \par \par \uc2  2125GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr4302c9l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
