\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Fed Buying Pushes Dollar Higher Versus Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 1995\par 02:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-DJ)--The dollar is higher against the yen in early Tokyo trading Monday than its levels late in New York Friday, pushed higher by U.S. Federal Reserve dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders say. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars between 86.50-87.10 yen from 2350 GMT to 0010 GMT Monday in Tokyo, a trader said. \par \par \uc2  He said he could confirm that the Fed bought dollars at those levels during that time. \par \par \uc2  The Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed dollar-buying by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) earlier at around 86.60-65 yen, another trader said. \par \par \uc2  Rumors that the Fed bought the dollar for yen, and even for the Deutsche mark, were heard early in Asian dealings, a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0033 GMT, the dollar is trading at 86.85 yen, down from 87.15 yen around 0001 GMT but above 86.55 yen in New York late Friday. The dollar was quoted at 89.13 yen late in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at 1.3765 marks, lower than 1.3783 marks around 0001 GMT but above 1.3735 marks late Friday in New York. The dollar was at 1.4080 marks in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is trading at 63.09 yen, down from 63.23 yen around 0001 GMT but above 63.01 yen in New York late Friday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Friday at 63.30 yen. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.6210, up from $1.6195 around 0001 GMT but even with $1.6210 in New York late Friday. Sterling was at $1.6065 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's movements were volatile early in Asian dealings. One dealer described trading conditions as 'thin.' \par \par \uc2  That dealer said the dollar is likely to trade between 86.50-87.50 yen in Asia on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On Friday the dollar plummeted to an new modern low of 86.23 yen in North American trading, largely on market disappointment that the BOJ chose not to lower its official discount rate earlier the same day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ could reassess that decision as early as Tuesday, however, and go ahead with a discount rate cut of around 0.75 basis point, a trader said. \par \par \uc2  The discount rate currently stands at 1.75%, its lowest level ever. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-04-95 \par \par \uc2  0057GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr4302bfd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
