\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo: Dlr Mixed; BOJ Buying, Mkt Watching FOMC \b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 02:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-DJ)--The dollar is mixed in early Tokyo trading Tuesday from its levels late in New York Monday, with dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  helping to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said they don't expect the market to move much ahead of a meeting of the Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) in Washington later Tuesday and a meeting of the Deutsche Bundesbank's central council on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Though market players say they don't expect either \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to change interest rates, broad hints that Japan may cut its interest rates to boost the dollar by Finance Minister Masayoshi Takemura Monday has added some uncertainty to the picture, they say. \par \par \uc2  Around 0030 GMT, the dollar is trading at 89.58 yen, up from 89.50 yen around 0001 GMT and 89.45 yen in New York late Monday. The dollar was quoted at 88.73 yen late in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also trading at 1.4049 Deutsche marks, lower than 1.4065 marks around 0001 GMT and 1.4063 marks late Monday in New York. The dollar was at 1.4135 marks in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is trading at 63.76 yen, up from 63.33 yen around 0001 GMT but below 63.61 yen in New York late Monday. The mark was quoted late in Tokyo Monday at 62.77 yen. \par \par \uc2  Sterling is at $1.5975, up from $1.5970 around 0001 GMT and above $1.5960 in New York late Monday. Sterling was at $1.5943 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Traders say there has been a reduction in the volume of dollar-selling by Japanese corporations ahead of the fiscal year end Friday that has been cited recently as a major demand factor driving the yen up. \par \par \uc2  'I don't think that's really much of a factor anymore,' said a Japanese bank trader. As a result, he said the dollar could float up a bit in the near term, though he noted it will have to get through heavy selling interest just below 90.00 yen to go appreciably higher. \par \par \uc2  The bank trader estimated the dollar will trade in ranges of 89.30-89.80 yen and 1.4020-1.4080 mark in Tokyo time Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the BOJ has been buying dollars steadily in an effort to sustain the dollar above the 89.50-yen level. The dollar rose late in Tokyo Monday after the BOJ began buying dollars aggressively just before Takemura's extraordinary press conference. \par \par \uc2  They said Takemura's comments are also supplying the dollar with a bit of support. They said Takemura's remarks have raised the possibility of international exchange rate coordination to support the dollar. \par \par \uc2  'I don't think it's very likely,' a Japanese bank trader said, 'but I don't think the market can just ignore (the possibility) either.' \par \par \uc2  Even though U.S. short-term rates already enjoy a substantial premium over comparable Japanese rates - the Fed Funds rate is now around 6% versus 2.16% for Japan's overnight call rate - traders say it will probably take more than lower Japanese rates to restore confidence in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Japan's investors have lost hundreds of millions of dollars in recent years due to exchange rate losses, and are now loath to chase potentially higher interest rate yields overseas, they say. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-03-95 \par \par \uc2  0049GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011030dr3s002zo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
