\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr Mixed As Mkt Awaits  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Meetings: World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By ALAN S. CULLISON \par \uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 23:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (AP-DJ)--The dollar fell back against the Deutsche mark Monday, amid profit-taking and a growing skepticism that the U.S. and German central banks will move their key interest rates this week. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar rallied from its lows against the yen on rumors of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  during Asian dealings and on hints that Japan might consider another cut in interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Mayoshi Takemura Monday pledged a 'flexible monetary policy' to counter recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market instability, taken by some to mean that Japan may soon resort to cutting its nearly rock-bottom interest rates in an effort to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit an intraday high of 89.75 yen on speculation that Japanese rates could fall. \par \par \uc2  The dollar could get even more of a boost if the Federal Reserve's Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) decides Tuesday to hike U.S. interest rates and if the Deutsche Bundesbank votes to cut its rates at a policy-setting meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But traders said the overwhelming consensus in the market is that neither \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is concerned enough about the recent weakness in the dollar to move interest rates this week. \par \par \uc2  Large U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds were rumored to have been big sellers of the dollar during U.S. trading Monday, as the dollar dropped about a pfennig against the mark. \par \par \uc2  'I think that on Thursday morning people are expecting that the dollar will take a hit when the Bundesbank doesn't ease rates,' said Win Thin, senior economist with IDEA analytic service in New York. 'So they thought they would get out of dollars before that.' \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the dollar was quoted at 1.4063 Deutsche marks, down from 1.4176 marks late Friday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also quoted at 89.45 yen, up from 88.98 yen. Sterling was trading at $1.5960, up from $1.5935. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-03-95 \par \par \uc2  2142GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011030dr3r002vl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
