\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Dlr Up Slightly, Market Awaits U.S. Data \b0\par\par\uc2  By MARI PFEIFFER \par \uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 07:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-DJ)--Unwilling to oust the dollar from narrow bands, dealers in the Asia-Pacific region Tuesday engaged in a mixture of dollar short-covering, and profit-taking in the Deutsche mark and yen, leaving the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  modestly higher. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers mentioned rumors of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through Singapore-based banks, but couldn't confirm the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves. \par \par \uc2  'It wouldn't be surprising, though,' said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Tokyo. 'There have been rumors since (Monday) that central banks, including the BOJ, have been checking rates and occasionally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from fluctuating wildly.' \par \par \uc2  Prospects of wild fluctuations Tuesday were remote, as dealers are waiting mostly for important U.S. economic indicators, said a dealer at a Japanese commercial bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  U.S. February retail sales data are due for release Tuesday followed by the February producer price index (PPI) on Wednesday and the February consumer price index (CPI) on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0600 GMT, the dollar is quoted at 90.89 yen, above 90.73 yen late Monday in New York and 90.45 yen late Monday in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at 1.4095 Deutsche marks, higher than 1.4065 marks late Monday in New York and 1.4068 marks in London Monday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is quoted at 64.48 yen, down from 64.50 yen in New York late Monday but above 64.29 yen in London late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed the dollar's lead, moving in familiar ranges amid a lack of fresh incentives. The Philippine peso remained under pressure, while the Malaysian ringgit too, fell back. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-03-95 \par \par \uc2  0605GMT \par \par \uc2  1046 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3e01ss7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
