\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Debt -3-: Rumors Of  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  After U.S. Jobs \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 09:27\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Repeating statements he made earlier in the week, Masahiko Komura, head of the Economic Planning Agency, said in an interview with the Nihon Keizai Shimbun it is his strong hope that the Bank of Japan will cut its official discount rate soon to cope with the yen's sharp appreciation. (See CMR page 4274). The discount rate is the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's charges on loans to banks and is currently at the record low of 1.75%. Trade and industry minister Ryutaro Hashimoto also said he hopes monetary authorities will make further efforts to combat the yen's rise and the government should expedite implementation of its public-works spending plan and large-scale supplementary budget as well. (See CMR page 4205). There were rumors that world central banks may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after the 1330 GMT release of U.S. employment data for February. This temporarily weighed on Japanese debt prices as a higher dollar would ease pressure on the Bank of Japan to cut rates. \par \par \uc2  Late Friday in Tokyo the dollar is 91.15 yen, up from 90.50 yen in New York late Thursday and down from 91.60 yen in Tokyo late Thursday. Participants will be looking at the U.S. jobs data for clues about whether or not the Federal Reserve will tighten monetary policy further. Economists look for non-farm payrolls to rise 239,000 in February, with the civilian jobless rate dropping to 5.6% from 5.7% the month before. On the supply side, few issuers are expected before the end of the fiscal year. But Mitsui Fudosan Co., Toa Steel Co. and Orix Corp. may offer bonds in the next couple of weeks, underwriters say. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 03-10-95 \par \par \uc2  0327EST \par \par \uc2  4077 4153 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011024dr3a00uc0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
