\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr beyond rescue without support measures - traders. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tatsuo Ito \par \uc2 610 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 8 (Reuter) - The beleaguered dollar, down more than seven percent against the yen in a week, could be drawn into a further downward spiral unless major nations use determined measures to support it, Tokyo dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Futile \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks and the lack of other effective measures to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far have reinforced views that the dollar's fall could continue unhindered. The problems of the U.S. budget deficit and Japan's trade surplus that have been behind the dollar's weakness in the past are once again resurfacing as factors, they said. \par \par \uc2  "This (dollar fall) reflects failure by both the United States and Japan to resolve their own economic problems that have been around for about 10 years," said Kinji Mutoh, deputy head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Dresdner Bank AG's Tokyo branch. The dollar plunged to a record low of 88.75 yen in mid-afternoon Tokyo trade on Wednesday. Dealers said the battered dollar could continue to move into uncharted waters for a while. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. senate last week failed to pass a constitutional amendment for a balanced budget plan. Meanwhile, Japan is still running a vast trade surplus. \par \par \uc2  Trade talks with Washington on autos and auto parts, which account for about 60 percent of Japan's surplus with the U.S., remain unresolved. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is signalling that Japan should speed up its efforts to deregulate the economy and increase its imports," said Mutoh. "Amid the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil across the world, Japan is the only country that complains about the appreciation of its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  A strong yen tends to hurt Japan's export industries by making Japanese goods more expensive abroad and eroding the value of dollar-denominated earnings. \par \par \uc2  But "in the present climate, Japan could be forced to accept a higher yen to the point where Japan's trade acounts would be balanced through an increase in imports," said Hiroshi Yabuta, a chief option dealer at Yasuda Trust and Banking. \par \par \uc2  "The mark could maintain its strength as long as turmoil in the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system persists, which means that the dollar has leeway to fall further against the mark and the yen," said Shinichi Abe, manager at Nikko Securities. \par \par \uc2  A possible rise in inflation in Germany following Tuesday's wage hike agreement could make it hard for the Bundesbank to take coordinated steps on interest rates, he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at 1.3555/65 marks at 0720 GMT after hitting a new record low of 1.3450 marks in Tokyo's afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Some Japanese car makers were seen to have sold dollars overnight through options instruments, which accelerated falls as bank traders joined in selling dollars for hedging purposes. \par \par \uc2  A bank dealer in Tokyo said there was talk that Middle East nations were trying to reduce the amount of oil income they receive in dollars and increase the proportion of marks, weakening dollar sentiment further. \par \par \uc2  Selling was also sparked by a New York Times report suggesting U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin was reluctant to take part in concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government said it would consider new economic measures to deal with the yen's rise, but gave no details. \par \par \uc2  "We cannot say what the government will do regarding this issue. However, we must cooperate closely with other nations and discuss the necessary steps we need to take," Chief Cabinet Secretary Kozo Igarashi said. \par \par \uc2  "These comments sound like they are incapable of doing anthing to cope with the yen's rise," said Dresdner's Mutoh. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr3800hwo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
