\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar stays weak in Asia despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 7 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets late on Tuesday to try to arrest the dollar's frenetic slide, but Asian dealers said the overall trend remained downwards. \par \par \uc2  In afternoon trade in Tokyo, dealers traded dollars for around 92.78 yen and 1.4028 marks, slightly weaker than its closing levels in New York on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Trade in Asia was relatively quiet until the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but market analysts said this was just a temporary respite, and there was little hope that the dollar would bounce back. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan appeared to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  first at under 92.70 yen, and later at around 92.60 yen. Then the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped in, buying U.S. and selling Singapore dollars at around 1.4290. \par \par \uc2  However, selling pressure from U.S. funds and other foreign operators was relentless, and there was a slew of exporters offering to sell at 93 yen. \par \par \uc2  "Until the (European) Exchange Rate Mechanism troubles are solved, the U.S. demonstrates its stance on the dollar more clearly and the Mexican peso stabilises, the basic trend will not change," said Yumiko Iijima, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at MMS International. \par \par \uc2  Overnight the dollar had slumped to a record postwar low of 92.45 yen, as doubts grew about the Federal Reserve's commitment to fighting inflation. \par \par \uc2  This was compounded by worries over Mexico, with some fearing that the Treasury has limited \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to defend the dollar as some of its resources were allocated to the $20 billion U.S. rescue package for Mexico. \par \par \uc2  Also, the mark continued to draw strength against the weaker European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after Spain and Portugal were forced to devalue the peseta and the escudo after these two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell below their floor in Europe's exchange rate mechanism. \par \par \uc2  However, though \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  put the brakes on dollar selling, for a while, the failure last week of central banks to prevent the slide means the dollar will likely fall further in the medium term. \par \par \uc2  "I think the downtrend will continue," said a Tokyo chief dealer at a British clearing bank. \par \par \uc2  "The market's exhausted, but the general investment flows will continue to go against the dollar," he said. \par \par \uc2  The soaring yen set off alarm bells in Japanese ministries, which are concerned that it could slice into the revenues of the country's exporters. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday morning, some demanded action from the Bank of Japan, and their calls were later answered when the bank stepped into the market during the afternoon session to buy dollars and sell yen. \par \par \uc2  "We want the monetary authorities to make further and more serious attempts to cope with the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  situation," said trade and industry minister Ryutaro Hashimoto. \par \par \uc2  The Economic Planning Agency agreed. \par \par \uc2  "Although (in general) interest rate cuts are not made for the sake of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I want (the Bank of Japan) to consider fully such action," said EPA minister Masahiko Komura. \par \par \uc2  Nikko Research Center released a report on Tuesday saying a dollar rate averaging 95 yen in the fiscal year starting April 1 would cut Japan's 1995/96 gross domestic product growth by 0.3 of a percentage point. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr3700llj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
