\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Roundup: Dlr Falters Again, BOJ Comes In Late \b0\par\par\uc2  By MARI PFEIFFER \par \uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 07:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-DJ)--Calm returned to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday in Asia, until U.S. funds came in the market to sell the dollar late in the day, prompting the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The BOJ bought dollars at 92.60-.70 yen around 0600 GMT, traders said. 'It looks like the BOJ is really serious about trying to prevent the dollar from falling below 92.50 yen,' one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered overnight borrowing rates for the first time in three weeks, from 30% to 22%. The peso fell on the back of robust demand for dollars from importers and manufacturers, and dealers are expecting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try recent highs again soon. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Hong Kong dollar (HK$), while steady against the U.S. dollar slipped lower versus other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0608 GMT, the dollar is quoted at 92.64 yen, below 92.80 yen late Monday in New York but up from 92.55 yen late Monday in London. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is at 1.4017 Deutsche marks, lower than 1.4048 marks late Monday in New York but above 1.3975 marks in London Monday. \par \par \uc2  The mark is quoted at 66.09 yen, up from 66.06 yen in New York late Monday but below 66.23 yen in London late Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-03-95 \par \par \uc2  0611GMT 