\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr Hits New Lows In Asia, Fragility Emphasized: Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By MARI PFEIFFER \par \uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1995\par 08:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (AP-DJ)--The forces that pushed the dollar down in Asian hours Monday to new postwar lows versus the yen and near-record lows against the Deutsche mark will stay in place for the near-term, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  Persistent worries over the fate of the Mexican economy and the pressure the Deutsche mark's strength has placed on the exchange-rate mechanism (ERM) of the European Monetary System (EMS) will continue to plague the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week. \par \par \uc2  Even massive, concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the world's central banks won't halt the dollar from sliding further. Traders said they expect the dollar may fall as low as 91.00 yen and below 1.3870 marks in the next 24 hours. \par \par \uc2  '\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always small compared to market flows overall,' said Chris Calderwood, economist at BZW Securities (Japan) Ltd. in Tokyo. 'By comparison what (central banks) do is just a drop in the ocean. What's more important is that it has to be well-timed.' \par \par \uc2  Market sources said 16 central banks participated in massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday to halt the dollar from sliding further against its major counterparts. But many dealers have since said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ineffective. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen to new postwar lows against the yen early Monday in Asian dealings, hitting 92.75 yen, despite what traders said was probably intermittent dollar-buying by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Though in the near-term, continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. Federal Reserve and other major central banks is likely to continue, some analysts suggest more is needed. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-03-95 \par \par \uc2  0705GMT \par \par \uc2  1137 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr3601izc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
